/** @dir Lib/eacp/Video
    Video recording and playback (namespace eacp::Video). Built where
    EACP_HAS_CAPTURE is on, except iOS and Android. There is no umbrella
    header: include the piece you use.

    - Recording: VideoRecorder writes a View to H.264 (.mov or .mp4) in one of
      three CaptureMode tiers. Snapshot needs no permission but leaves a
      WebView blank; Screen records the whole window and needs Screen Recording
      permission on macOS; GpuDirect is for a GPUView only. start() and stop()
      run on the main thread, pushAudio() on the audio thread, and the
      VideoRecorder must outlive the Async stop() returns.
    - Playback: Decoder is synchronous and policy-free; FrameStream runs it
      ahead on a thread and answers frameAt(time); Player is a clock the
      caller advances. To draw, use VideoView.
*/
